             mlx5_ib_stage_sys_error_notifier_cleanup),
before STAGE_CREATE(MLX5_IB_STAGE_IB_REG, ...).

Reason: The new notifier is registered before IB_REG (device registration) and cleaned after IB_REG (device unregistration). This ensures that sys_error events (including those forwarded from the slave) are received throughout the entire unload process, allowing the driver to detect the error, abort pending UMR operations, and avoid the hang.

